\section{Covariant Conservation of Energy-Momentum}

Let $(\mathcal{M}, g_{\mu\nu})$ be a pseudo-Riemannian manifold with ADM
$3+1$ decomposition. The GRMHD stress-energy tensor is
\begin{equation}
T^{\mu\nu}
=
(\rho h + b^2) u^\mu u^\nu
+
\left(p + \frac{b^2}{2}\right) g^{\mu\nu}
-
b^\mu b^\nu.
\end{equation}

\subsection{Gauss--Stokes Theorem in Curved Spacetime}
For any compact 4-volume $\mathcal{V}$ with boundary $\partial\mathcal{V}$,
the covariant divergence satisfies
\begin{equation}
\int_{\mathcal{V}}
\nabla_\mu T^{\mu\nu} \sqrt{-g}\, d^4x
=
\oint_{\partial\mathcal{V}}
T^{\mu\nu} n_\mu \sqrt{|\gamma|}\, d^3x.
\end{equation}

If the boundary fluxes telescope exactly, the left-hand side vanishes.

\subsection{Discrete Conservation Under HRSC Fluxes}
